# Line endings
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true at the system level, which
# rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. That fights Prettier/ESLint, makes
# whole-file diffs out of one-line changes, and differs from what CI (Linux)
# sees. These rules win over core.autocrlf, so every clone — Windows included —
# gets LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never run line-ending or diff conversion on these.
# text=auto detects most of them by content, but being explicit means a
# misdetection can't corrupt a texture.
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.jar   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
